  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YAL - Kwanga - Kizimba Social Enterprise</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agribusiness/ Animal Husbandry .Beneficiaries; YALI Youth 312 of which 159 are women. ..The grant will be used to implement a goat breeding and rearing business in that will be a catalyst for information sharing and training in modern farming. The breeding program will introduce a cross breed of local goats with improved Savannah bucks and a training of farmers and students on basic modern farm management which will increase the income of 50 targeted farmers. The goal of the project is to increase the income of 50 farmers as well as train 50 youth farmers on agribusiness with practical skills from goat breeding to cash-flow management. ..The grant funds will be used to: (a) protect livestock through the construction of pens and watering hole; (b) purchase of breeding bucks to enhance goat breed; (c) training of 150 students and 50 farmers; and (d) technical assistance from livestock development specialist. .</narrative>
  </description>
